WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.867
Bottom line: treat Copilot Autopilot as a bounded standing role, not a better chatbot.

00:00:06.867 --> 00:00:15.333
Approve one private-preview pilot only where a named leader owns the goal, access boundary, cost and outcomes.

00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:20.767
The shift is from asking for an answer to assigning a standing role.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:29.167
Autopilot was announced with identity, memory, a computer and workspace; leaders still set objectives and boundaries.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.533
That changes governance, not just productivity.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:44.400
Foundry provides an architectural lens, not proof that every implementation is identical: identity establishes the role, while capability can change.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:52.367
The organization controls interactions, access and actions, and an accountable manager remains essential.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.967
Pilot one recurring workflow with one team and one accountable owner.

00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:04.633
Reuse a blueprint for logic, but scope each instance to its own permissions and assignment.

00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:12.867
Because Copilot Autopilot remains private preview, require a stop condition and outcome review before expansion.
